6. Consider the curve defined by \(2 y^{3}+6 x^{2} y-12 x^{2}+6 y=1\).
\begin{itemize}
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Show that \(\frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{4 x-2 x y}{x^{2}+y^{2}+1}\).
\item[(b)] Write an equation of each horizontal tangent line to the curve.
\item[(c)] The line through the origin with slope -1 is tangent to the curve at point \(P\). Find the \(x-\) and \(y\)-coordinates of point \(P\).
\end{itemize}
\item[(a)] \(6 y^{2} \frac{d y}{d x}+6 x^{2} \frac{d y}{d x}+12 x y-24 x+6 \frac{d y}{d x}=0\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{d y}{d x}\left(6 y^{2}+6 x^{2}+6\right)=24 x-12 x y \\
& \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{24 x-12 x y}{6 x^{2}+6 y^{2}+6}=\frac{4 x-2 x y}{x^{2}+y^{2}+1}
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)] \(\frac{d y}{d x}=0\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
& 4 x-2 x y=2 x(2-y)=0 \\
& x=0 \text { or } y=2
\end{aligned}
\]
When \(x=0,2 y^{3}+6 y=1 ; y=0.165\)
There is no point on the curve with \(y\) coordinate of 2.
\(y=0.165\) is the equation of the only horizontal tangent line.
\item[(c)] \(y=-x\) is equation of the line.
\[
\begin{aligned}
& 2(-x)^{3}+6 x^{2}(-x)-12 x^{2}+6(-x)=1 \\
& -8 x^{3}-12 x^{2}-6 x-1=0 \\
& x=-1 / 2, \quad y=1 / 2 \\
& - \text { or- } \\
& \frac{d y}{d x}=-1 \\
& 4 x-2 x y=-x^{2}-y^{2}-1 \\
& 4 x+2 x^{2}=-x^{2}-x^{2}-1 \\
& 4 x^{2}+4 x+1=0 \\
& x=-1 / 2, \quad y=1 / 2
\end{aligned}
\]
